=encoding utf8

=head1 NAME

std/proc - Process execution, environment, and signals.

=head1 SYNOPSIS

  from std/proc import Proc, Env, sleep;

  let pid := Proc.pid();
  let home := Env.get("HOME", "");

  let res := Proc.run(
    "perl",
    [ "-e", "print qq<ok\\n>;" ]
  );

  let seen := 0;
  Proc.onsignal( "USR1", function () {
    seen++;
  } );
  Proc.kill( "USR1", Proc.pid() );

  sleep(0.1);

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This module provides OS process helpers backed by C<IPC::Run3>,
environment variable helpers, signal send/receive primitives,
process-identification helpers, and process exit.

=head2 Exports

=over

=item C<Proc>

Static methods:

=over

=item * C<pid()>

Returns the current process id.

=item * C<< exit(code?) >>

Exits the current process.

=item * C<< run(command, argv?, options?) >>

Options include C<stdin>, C<capture_stdout>, C<capture_stderr>,
and C<merge_stderr>. Also supports C<env> injection, C<cwd>, and
C<timeout>.

Returns a result (dict).

=item * C<< run_async(command, argv?, options?) >>

Awaitable version of C<run>. Returns a C<Task> resolving to the same
result dict.

=item * C<< pipeline(commands, options?) >>

Runs commands in sequence, piping captured stdout from each step
to the next step's stdin. Options include C<stdin>, C<capture_stderr>,
C<merge_stderr>, C<env>, C<cwd>, and C<timeout>.

=item * C<< pipeline_async(commands, options?) >>

Awaitable version of C<pipeline>. Returns a C<Task> resolving to the
same result dict.

=item * C<is_success(result)>

=item * C<status_text(result)>

=item * C<kill(String signal, Number pid?)>

=item * C<onsignal(String signal, Function callback)>

=back

=item C<Env>

Static methods:

=over

=item * C<get(String name, Any default?)>

=item * C<set(String name, String value)>

=item * C<remove(String name)>

=back

=item C<sleep>

Function:

=over

=item * C<< sleep(seconds) >>

Sleeps for the given number of seconds. Fractional seconds are allowed.

=item * C<< sleep_async(seconds) >>

Returns an awaitable C<Task> that completes after the requested delay
without blocking the async scheduler.

=back

=back

